      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-hostages-act-1989-article-5",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "5 1.",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-hostages-act-1989#article-5"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-hostages-act-1989.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-hostages-act-1989.pdf, p.14",
      "values:originalText": "Each State Party shall take such measures as may be necessary to\nestablish its jurisdiction over any of the offences set forth in article 1 which are\ncommitted:\n\nInternational Convention Against The Taking Of Hostages  Schedule\n\nCrimes (Hostages) Act 1989\nCompilation date: 10/3/16\nRegistered: 25/5/16\n\n(a)\nin its territory or on board a ship or aircraft registered in that State;\n(b)\nby any of its nationals or, if that State considers it appropriate, by\nthose stateless persons who have their habitual residence in its\nterritory;\n(c)\nin order to compel that State to do or abstain from doing any act; or\n(d)\nwith respect to a hostage who is a national of that State, if that State\nconsiders it appropriate.\n2.\nEach State Party shall likewise take such measures as may be necessary to\nestablish its jurisdiction over the offences set forth in article 1 in cases where\nthe alleged offender is present in its territory and it does not extradite him to any\nof the States mentioned in paragraph 1 of this article.\n3.\nThis Convention does not exclude any criminal jurisdiction exercised in\naccordance with internal law.",
      "skos:definition": "Each State Party shall take such measures as may be necessary to\nestablish its jurisdiction over any of the offences set forth in article 1 which are\ncommitted:\n\nInternational Convention Against The Taking Of Hostages  Schedule\n\nCrimes (Hostages) Act 1989\nCompilation date: 10/3/16\nRegistered: 25/5/16\n\n(a)\nin its territory or on board a ship or aircraft registered in that State;\n(b)\nby any of its nationals or, if that State considers it appropriate, by\nthose stateless persons who have their habitual residence in its\nterritory;\n(c)\nin order to compel that State to do or abstain from doing any act; or\n(d)\nwith respect to a hostage who is a national of that State, if that State\nconsiders it appropriate.\n2.\nEach State Party shall likewise take such measures as may be necessary to\nestablish its jurisdiction over the offences set forth in article 1 in cases where\nthe alleged offender is present in its territory and it does not extradite him to any\nof the States mentioned in paragraph 1 of this article.\n3.\nThis Convention does not exclude any criminal jurisdiction exercised in\naccordance with internal law.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-hostages-act-1989-article-5-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-hostages-act-1989-article-5-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "24f3c00bcccfd1d5898dbcc76e8889bb071ddb1bc024d89754a61c40ecec4303",
      "skos:note": "Establish jurisdiction over certain crimes committed in its territory or by its nationals."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-hostages-act-1989#article-5",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "5 1.",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 14,
      "values:originalText": "Each State Party shall take such measures as may be necessary to\nestablish its jurisdiction over any of the offences set forth in article 1 which are\ncommitted:\n\nInternational Convention Against The Taking Of Hostages  Schedule\n\nCrimes (Hostages) Act 1989\nCompilation date: 10/3/16\nRegistered: 25/5/16\n\n(a)\nin its territory or on board a ship or aircraft registered in that State;\n(b)\nby any of its nationals or, if that State considers it appropriate, by\nthose stateless persons who have their habitual residence in its\nterritory;\n(c)\nin order to compel that State to do or abstain from doing any act; or\n(d)\nwith respect to a hostage who is a national of that State, if that State\nconsiders it appropriate.\n2.\nEach State Party shall likewise take such measures as may be necessary to\nestablish its jurisdiction over the offences set forth in article 1 in cases where\nthe alleged offender is present in its territory and it does not extradite him to any\nof the States mentioned in paragraph 1 of this article.\n3.\nThis Convention does not exclude any criminal jurisdiction exercised in\naccordance with internal law."
    },
