    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-hostages-act-1989-article-8",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "8 1.",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-hostages-act-1989#article-8"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-hostages-act-1989.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-hostages-act-1989.pdf, p.16",
      "values:originalText": "The State Party in the territory of which the alleged offender is found\nshall, if it does not extradite him, be obliged, without exception whatsoever and\nwhether or not the offence was committed in its territory, to submit the case to\nits competent authorities for the purpose of prosecution, through proceedings in\naccordance with the laws of that State. Those authorities shall take their\ndecision in the same manner as in the case of any ordinary offence of a grave\nnature under the law of that State.\n\nInternational Convention Against The Taking Of Hostages  Schedule\n\nCrimes (Hostages) Act 1989\nCompilation date: 10/3/16\nRegistered: 25/5/16\n\n2.\nAny person regarding whom proceedings are being carried out in\nconnexion with any of the offences set forth in article 1 shall be guaranteed fair\ntreatment at all stages of the proceedings, including enjoyment of all the rights\nand guarantees provided by the law of the State in the territory of which he is\npresent.",
      "skos:definition": "The State Party in the territory of which the alleged offender is found\nshall, if it does not extradite him, be obliged, without exception whatsoever and\nwhether or not the offence was committed in its territory, to submit the case to\nits competent authorities for the purpose of prosecution, through proceedings in\naccordance with the laws of that State. Those authorities shall take their\ndecision in the same manner as in the case of any ordinary offence of a grave\nnature under the law of that State.\n\nInternational Convention Against The Taking Of Hostages  Schedule\n\nCrimes (Hostages) Act 1989\nCompilation date: 10/3/16\nRegistered: 25/5/16\n\n2.\nAny person regarding whom proceedings are being carried out in\nconnexion with any of the offences set forth in article 1 shall be guaranteed fair\ntreatment at all stages of the proceedings, including enjoyment of all the rights\nand guarantees provided by the law of the State in the territory of which he is\npresent.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-hostages-act-1989-article-8-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-hostages-act-1989-article-8-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-hostages-act-1989-article-8-logic-alleninterval-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-hostages-act-1989-article-8-logic-argumentation-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "c3bc16045db341e734d3b6cccf984b9419ca582b64584602a2f545c510f5c481",
      "skos:note": "The State Party must submit the case to its competent authorities for prosecution."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-hostages-act-1989#article-8",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "8 1.",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 16,
      "values:originalText": "The State Party in the territory of which the alleged offender is found\nshall, if it does not extradite him, be obliged, without exception whatsoever and\nwhether or not the offence was committed in its territory, to submit the case to\nits competent authorities for the purpose of prosecution, through proceedings in\naccordance with the laws of that State. Those authorities shall take their\ndecision in the same manner as in the case of any ordinary offence of a grave\nnature under the law of that State.\n\nInternational Convention Against The Taking Of Hostages  Schedule\n\nCrimes (Hostages) Act 1989\nCompilation date: 10/3/16\nRegistered: 25/5/16\n\n2.\nAny person regarding whom proceedings are being carried out in\nconnexion with any of the offences set forth in article 1 shall be guaranteed fair\ntreatment at all stages of the proceedings, including enjoyment of all the rights\nand guarantees provided by the law of the State in the territory of which he is\npresent."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-hostages-act-1989-article-8-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:crimes-hostages-act-1989-article-8"
